// PORT-PENDING 0425 crates-jet-sema-src-sema-checkervalidate-module-group: crates/jet-sema/src/Sema/CheckerValidate.rs:1-687
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! D-VALIDATE1 (ratified 2026-07-12, card #506): `validate { … }` in-body
//RS //! block. See Docs/spec/syntax-decisions.md for the full ratified law.
//RS //!
//RS //! Runs pre-registration, same timing as
//RS //! `CheckerFieldPolicy::process_computed_fields` (D-FIELDPOL1): for each
//RS //! struct with a non-empty `validate_block`,
//RS //!   1. check every rule statement's shape — it must be exactly
//RS //!      `check(cond, at: field, "msg")` (E0353); `field` must name a real
//RS //!      field of the struct (E0354);
//RS //!   2. rewrite bare `Ident`s in `cond`/`msg` that name a sibling field to
//RS //!      `value.<field>` — reuses `CheckerFieldPolicy::rewrite_field_refs`,
//RS //!      the exact substitution D-FIELDPOL1 computed fields use for
//RS //!      `self.<field>`, with the receiver renamed to `value`;
//RS //!   3. synthesize `fn validate(value: Self) -> Self ![FieldError] { … }`
//RS //!      as a plain (non-trait) `impl Type { }` block appended to the
//RS //!      module, `is_pure: true` — the existing `pure fn` purity pass
//RS //!      (S60/E3401) then enforces "a rule may reference only fields and
//RS //!      pure calls" over the whole synthesized body for free, no separate
//RS //!      purity pass needed.
//RS //!
//RS //! The in-body block + `Type.validate(value)` standalone entry point are
//RS //! wired. Typed decoding and validation share the owner-ratified accumulated
//RS //! `[FieldError]` result contract.
//RS 
